; The implementer's fixture: `key = value` lines, one object a line, with
; spaces allowed around the `=` (the engine skips them). The newline is not
; named: an entry is three tokens and needs no line end to stop at, so
; comments and blank lines cost nothing and a value cannot hold a space.
settings = *entry             ; @array
entry    = key "=" value      ; @object key value
key      = ( TX )
value    = ( TX )
